Python implementation developed 2026-11-05 through 2026-11-13: streaming
upload, balanced segmentation, timeline restoration, full raw responses,
PyAV processing, SILK decoding and host-independent budget/client injection.
The protocol core is mirrored from Tiance's independent audio_transcribe
tool. Each host ships its own copy and does not load the other at runtime.

The backend installs upstream PyAV 16.0.1 as a Python dependency. It does
not ship or load the tool's custom audio-only PyAV build. PyAV and bundled
FFmpeg libraries retain the notices in their installed distributions.

The SILK decoder from kn007/silk-v3-decoder retains the MIT wrapper and
Skype SDK licenses, source revision and binary hash in vendor/silk/.
